    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Sun is a 57-year-old physician by training and political leader who comes for his yearly preventive visit, timed with the day-8 infusion of cycle 6, which he had this morning. The cold of three weeks ago cleared within a week without fever. He has been working most days and has kept his weight steady with the dietitian&apos;s advice. He meets the palliative care team every three to four weeks and has talked with them about what matters most to him. He asked which preventive services still make sense for him now, and wants the vaccines that protect him during treatment. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic adult preventive visit, age 57</td></tr><tr><td>Cancer treatment</td><td>Cycle 6 of gemcitabine, cisplatin and durvalumab; day-8 dose today</td></tr><tr><td>Recent illness</td><td>Cold cleared within a week</td></tr><tr><td>Weight</td><td>Steady at about 59 kg</td></tr><tr><td>His question</td><td>Which preventive services still make sense now</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient on the clinic tablet before the visit and reviewed with him by Dr. Huang. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Fair; tired in the afternoons, but working most days</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Supported by colleagues and his household; talks openly with the palliative care team</td></tr><tr><td>Substance use</td><td>Alcohol rarely, at formal dinners; none since starting treatment; no drugs</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Never smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Walks 30 minutes most days</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Small frequent meals and a protein drink each day, as the dietitian advised</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Six to seven hours; occasional night waking</td></tr><tr><td>Infection precautions</td><td>Hand hygiene; avoids crowds in the week after day-8 doses; has a thermometer</td></tr><tr><td>Safety at home</td><td>Feels safe; smoke alarm working; no firearm at home</td></tr><tr><td>Road safety</td><td>Wears a seat belt; is driven to most meetings</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

