<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan adjusted to his advanced cancer, as he asked. Vaccines that protect him during treatment are given today. Cancer screening tests whose benefit takes years to appear (colon, prostate) are not offered now because of his metastatic cancer, after discussion with him. He has never had an HIV test and agreed to one. [S]<list><item>Inactivated influenza, COVID-19 and PCV20 pneumococcal vaccines today.</item><item>First recombinant zoster vaccine dose at the next visit.</item><item>HIV test today.</item><item>No live vaccines while on treatment.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Gallbladder adenocarcinoma, stage IVB, on chemoimmunotherapy (C23)</content>. Liver edge smaller on examination; weight steady; ECOG 1. Treatment continues with Dr. Choi. [S]<list><item>Cycle 7 as booked; restaging CT after cycle 7.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute viral upper respiratory infection (J06.9)</content>. Resolved. [S]<list><item>No further action.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>122/76 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 1; PHQ-9 tracked at oncology visits</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Drinks rarely; none since treatment began</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never screened; with metastatic gallbladder cancer the benefit of screening would not be realized, and he agreed not to pursue it now</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Discussed; not offered while he has metastatic cancer</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never smoked; he has CT scans of the chest every 2 to 3 months for his cancer</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not overweight; glucose 98 mg/dL at intake</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Never tested; once-in-a-lifetime test drawn today with his agreement</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Antibody negative at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Resolved infection at intake; HBV DNA monitored during treatment; vaccination not needed</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Inactivated vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Given today; immunocompromised adults may need an additional dose, to be reviewed with the oncology team</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 given today because chemotherapy suppresses his immunity; no further pneumococcal dose needed</td></tr><tr><td>Zoster vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine recommended for immunocompromised adults; first dose at the next visit, second one to two months later</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap after a hand cut five years ago</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 1924-1925 season (inactivated); COVID-19 vaccine, 1924-1925 formula; Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine (PCV20), for immunosuppression by chemotherapy [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Integration of Palliative Care Into Standard Oncology Care: American Society of Clinical Oncology Clinical Practice Guideline Update (2017); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Colorectal Cancer: Screening (2021); Adult Immunization Schedule by Medical Condition and Other Indication (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: HIV result by phone. Cycle 7 as booked. Oncology visit before cycle 8 with restaging CT; first zoster vaccine dose then. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 1924-10-26: before cycle 8: restaging CT, toxicity review, low magnesium, and the plan for maintenance durvalumab. [S]</paragraph></text>

