    <code code="42348-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Advance directives"/>
    <title>Advance Care Planning</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voluntary advance care planning discussion of about 25 minutes, with his consent, building on his conversations with the palliative care team. He named a health care agent, recorded in the confidential part of the chart and not named here. He wants to be told everything plainly and to make his own decisions while he can. He wants treatment that lets him keep working and thinking clearly; if his illness reached the point where he could no longer communicate and there was no prospect of recovery, he would not want to be kept alive on machines and would want comfort care. He chose to wait before completing a portable medical order form and will revisit it with the palliative care team. To be revisited when treatment changes. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
